{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghc7nbdoUag8n3ReNAow","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KF56h6cdofwJcu4kVmXro1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-sqwr_1lr/NOTES.md","content":"# Ring classifier construction\n\nIdea: compute s ≈ r² = x0² + x1², then test 0.16 ≤ s ≤ 0.5625.\n\n**Layer 1 (32 units):** for each coordinate i, sign σ∈{+,−} and knot t_j = j·0.75/8 (j=0..7),\nunit = relu(σ·x_i − t_j). Since relu(x−t)+relu(−x−t) = relu(|x|−t) for t ≥ 0, a weighted sum\nΣ_j c_j relu(|x_i|−t_j) with c_0 = h, c_j = 2h gives the piecewise-linear interpolant of x_i² at the\nknots (exact at knots, overestimate ≤ h²/4; beyond 0.75 it extends linearly, which is fine because\nthen r > 0.75 anyway).\n\n**Layer 2 (2 units used):** s = Σ c_j·h1 − h²/4 (offset centres the interpolation error to ±h²/4 ≈ ±0.0022).\nA = relu(s − m), B = relu(m − s), with m = (0.16+0.5625)/2, so A + B = |s − m|.\n\n**Output:** logit1 − logit0 = 100·(w − A − B), w = (0.5625−0.16)/2; positive exactly when s is in the band.\nExpected error is only a thin sliver near the two circles (~0.3% of points).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3072,"cache_read_input_tokens":2254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3072},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a414d59-57e5-48ac-b1e2-c407a055e11f","uuid":"c85d72ab-b1c7-4aaa-be79-bf332f2117f5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:54:42.969Z","request_id":"req_011Cghc7nEpPTJNPWyn67Pwm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KF56h6cdofwJcu4kVmXro1":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-sqwr_1lr/NOTES.md","content":"# Ring classifier construction\n\nIdea: compute s ≈ r² = x0² + x1², then test 0.16 ≤ s ≤ 0.5625.\n\n**Layer 1 (32 units):** for each coordinate i, sign σ∈{+,−} and knot t_j = j·0.75/8 (j=0..7),\nunit = relu(σ·x_i − t_j). Since relu(x−t)+relu(−x−t) = relu(|x|−t) for t ≥ 0, a weighted sum\nΣ_j c_j relu(|x_i|−t_j) with c_0 = h, c_j = 2h gives the piecewise-linear interpolant of x_i² at the\nknots (exact at knots, overestimate ≤ h²/4; beyond 0.75 it extends linearly, which is fine because\nthen r > 0.75 anyway).\n\n**Layer 2 (2 units used):** s = Σ c_j·h1 − h²/4 (offset centres the interpolation error to ±h²/4 ≈ ±0.0022).\nA = relu(s − m), B = relu(m − s), with m = (0.16+0.5625)/2, so A + B = |s − m|.\n\n**Output:** logit1 − logit0 = 100·(w − A − B), w = (0.5625−0.16)/2; positive exactly when s is in the band.\nExpected error is only a thin sliver near the two circles (~0.3% of points).\n"}}}
